WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.383
- [Narrator] Sour, salty, crunchy.

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.870
I think it's safe to say that
everybody loves a good pickle.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.860
There's a little shop
just outside of Philly

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.740
that takes pickles to a whole new level.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.573
- Welcome to Elsie's,

00:00:12.573 --> 00:00:15.060
the sandwich shop that uses
pickles instead of bread.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.773
Wanna try one, or two, or three?

00:00:17.773 --> 00:00:20.440
(playful music)

00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:27.183
(cheerful music)

00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:28.620
My name is Katherine Cohen,

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.870
and I am the head pickle proprietor

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.110
at Elsie's in Haddon Township, New Jersey.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.360
Elsie's was born out of necessity.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.560
Our mom is a cancer survivor

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.010
and was diagnosed with diabetes

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.890
and that was something that
she was really struggling with.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.850
We decided, as a family,
to start making our mom

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.960
sandwiches on pickles,
rather than on bread.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.630
We resurrected an old family recipe

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.360
that hadn't been used
in probably a decade,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.943
and we started from there.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.790
Part of the process

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.110
of making our Elsie's signature pickles

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.810
involved icing down the Kirby cucumbers,

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.350
adding sea salt, vinegar, onions, garlic,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.667
and that's all I can tell you

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.890
because my mom will not be happy

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.153
if I reveal what the recipe actually is.

00:01:22.616 --> 00:01:24.110
- Napkin's in the bag.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:25.233
You're all set, thank you.

00:01:25.233 --> 00:01:27.670
- [Katherine] Part of
the concept with Elsie's

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.690
was to create a sanctuary

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.770
for people that have dietary restrictions:

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.620
diabetes, celiac, keto, gluten-free.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.862
We found that there was a
need for a bread-alternative

00:01:39.862 --> 00:01:42.893
and the pickle sandwich
became very, very popular.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.685
One of our best-selling sandwiches

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:48.240
is the Elsie's famous Italian,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.130
which is ham, capocollo,
salami, provolone,

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.933
lettuce, tomato, onion.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.530
You can even get it
topped with Sriracha mayo,

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.363
hots, crushed potato chips.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.470
To bite into an Elsie's
signature pickle sandwich,

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.660
it really is heaven.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.590
It's crisp.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.770
It's crunchy.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.208
It really is a fantastic experience.

00:02:10.208 --> 00:02:11.530
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.888
- It's unlike anything
I've ever had before.

00:02:13.888 --> 00:02:15.700
- Very good.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.510
- Our other option is a cucumber roll-up,

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.640
and you can have the cucumber roll-ups

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.690
made with any sandwich topping you'd like.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.760
Both pickle and cucumber roll-ups

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.490
are served with a pair of chopsticks,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.030
so it's really a lot of fun to eat.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:32.060
We offer complimentary pickle brine.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.510
While you're at the shop,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.360
you're welcome to as
many pickle juice shots

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.563
as you can handle.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.180
People take a pickle
pilgrimage to come here.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.180
They have rerouted flights.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.920
They have driven from Toronto, Canada,

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.573
to experience Elsie's.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.510
It makes me feel awesome
because, at the core,

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.840
I'm really an old lady,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.678
and I just really love to feed people.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.011
(laughing)

